is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r7
diagnosis_text:
The issue is not a physical link failure but a control-plane outage on R7. The R6–R7 interlink (segment Y: R6 eth2 <-> R7 eth0, 67.0.0.0/8) is up at Layer 2/3 on both ends: R6 eth2 and R7 eth0 are UP/RUNNING with 67.1.1.1/8 and 67.1.1.2/8 assigned, and ethtool reports “Link detected: yes” on both interfaces. R6 can ping R7 (3/3 replies), further confirming L2/L3 connectivity.

OSPF adjacency is down because R7’s FRRouting/OSPF daemon is not running. On R6, “show ip ospf interface eth2” shows Neighbor Count 0. On R7, “show ip ospf neighbor” returns “ospfd is not running,” and systemd reports “frr.service … Active: failed.” R7’s running-config is effectively empty (no OSPF config), so no R7-region prefixes (17.x.x.x, 70.0.
